   "start": 296.97,
   "end": 300.2,
   "text": "Put the rent and the commute together, and you get a far more useful price."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 2 Geneva",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 31,
   "start": 301.11,
   "end": 301.34,
   "text": "2."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 2 Geneva",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 32,
   "start": 301.94,
   "end": 302.46,
   "text": "Geneva."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 2 Geneva",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 33,
   "start": 303.37,
   "end": 305.61,
   "text": "The Jet d'Eau gives the city its signature view."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 2 Geneva",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 34,
   "start": 306.17,
   "end": 309.59,
   "text": "Our central one-bedroom figure is about $2,900 a month,"
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 2 Geneva",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 35,
   "start": 309.95,
   "end": 311.34,
   "text": "level with Zurich once rounded."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 2 Geneva",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 36,
   "start": 311.86,
   "end": 314.29,
   "text": "Outside the centre, it's around $2,200."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 2 Geneva",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 37,
   "start": 314.95,
   "end": 316.94,
   "text": "Yet Geneva ranks two places higher."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 2 Geneva",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 38,
   "start": 317.65,
   "end": 320.92,
   "text": "That's another reason to keep the overall ranking separate from the rent comparison."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 2 Geneva",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 39,
   "start": 321.6,
   "end": 323.55,
   "text": "Matching rents don't mean matching living costs."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 2 Geneva",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 40,
   "start": 324.25,
   "end": 329.07,
   "text": "Before choosing between cities, compare your full budget in the currency you'll actually be paid in."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 2 Geneva",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 41,
   "start": 329.64,
   "end": 331.49,
   "text": "A neat dollar figure makes comparison easy."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 2 Geneva",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 42,
   "start": 332.4,
   "end": 334.73,
   "text": "Your own circumstances decide whether it's affordable."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 1 New York",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 43,
   "start": 336.53,
   "end": 336.81,
   "text": "1."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 1 New York",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 44,
   "start": 337.26,
   "end": 337.82,
   "text": "New York."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 1 New York",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 45,
   "start": 338.73,
   "end": 339.81,
   "text": "Remember that opening figure?"
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 1 New York",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 46,
   "start": 340.31,
   "end": 345.02,
   "text": "A city-centre one-bedroom averages roughly $4,500 a month in our snapshot."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 1 New York",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 47,
   "start": 345.93,
   "end": 346.96,
   "text": "Multiply that by 12"
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 1 New York",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 48,
   "start": 347.35,
   "end": 349.59,
   "text": "and you're at $54,000 a year."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 1 New York",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 50,
   "start": 350.68,
   "end": 354.9,
   "text": "Outside the centre, the estimate is around $3,000 a month, or $36,000 a year."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 1 New York",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 51,
   "start": 355.56,
   "end": 358.54,
   "text": "That's a difference of roughly $18,000 a year."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 1 New York",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 52,
   "start": 358.93,
   "end": 360.51,
   "text": "And that's before the rest of daily life."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 1 New York",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 53,
   "start": 361.25,
   "end": 364.2,
   "text": "So the layout, the daylight and the actual commute all matter."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 1 New York",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 54,
   "start": 364.81,
   "end": 365.99,
   "text": "The famous view is a bonus."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 1 New York",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 55,
   "start": 366.69,
   "end": 367.85,
   "text": "The bill arrives every month."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Number 1 New York",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 56,
   "start": 368.6,
   "end": 369.77,
   "text": "Would the address be worth it to you?"
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Closing question",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 57,
   "start": 371.55,
   "end": 375.34,
   "text": "Across these cities, the useful number is what you have left after the essentials."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Closing question",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 58,
   "start": 375.98,
   "end": 376.83,
   "text": "Compare like with like,"
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Closing question",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 59,
   "start": 377.15,
   "end": 377.92,
   "text": "include the commute,"
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Closing question",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 60,
   "start": 378.25,
   "end": 380.27,
   "text": "and treat any average as a starting point."
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Closing question",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 61,
   "start": 381.07,
   "end": 382.74,
   "text": "Which city would you pay a premium for?"
  },
  {
   "chapter": "Closing question",
   "src": "part_b",
   "idx": 62,
   "start": 383.43,
   "end": 387.47,
   "text": "Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for more comparisons of what your money actually buys."
  }
